    {
      "reviewtitle": "Not the Complete Book",
      "reviewbody": "This file is not the complete book (or even close), and the formatting of the file is extremely confusing (especially the page numbering).\n\nHere are two alternate versions. They are both imperfect, but at least they appear to be complete:\n1) https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.283716/\n2) https://archive.org/details/sacredbooksofthehindusvol11samkhyaphilosophynandalalsinha1915_202002/\n\nIn #1, the first few pages of the introduction are cut off on the edges, so words are missing. I don't know about the rest of the book; most of the pages look fine. At first glance it seems like a much better copy than #2, and in some regards it is, but often it is nearly unreadable, whereas the words are much more legible in #2. Unfortunately, the file size of #2 is over 400 MB, as opposed to about 40 MB for #1. (The \"PDF WITH TEXT\" download option for #2 is less than 200 MB and still readable but not quite as good as the full size version.)\n\nFinally, here is a very good copy of just the introduction alone, which I only include here in case someone wants to make an improved copy by splicing together parts from various files:\nhttps://archive.org/details/thesamkhyaphilosophysinha/The%20Samkhya%20Philosophy_Sinha_Introduction/",
      "stars": "0",
